INT. CARGO SHIP SICK BAY - NIGHT

A steel cabin the size of a closet. A table bolted to the floor. Storm light flickers. The hull groans.

DR. REUBEN ABARA, 40s, a ship's physician in a bloody apron, presses a pad to the wound in an unconscious sailor's side. The ship pitches. Instruments skid across the tray. He pins them with an elbow, clamps a vessel with his free hand, and wipes his brow on his shoulder.

An intercom speaker crackles on the wall.

FELIX (V.O.)
(crackling)
Sick bay, bridge. Doc, how is he?

Reuben leans toward the speaker without lifting his hands.

REUBEN
Bleeding. Lung's punctured. I need him on a ventilator and you've given me a bicycle pump.

FELIX (V.O.)
Nearest port is eleven hours.

REUBEN
He doesn't have eleven hours, Felix.

FELIX (V.O.)
I know. I'm the second mate. I'm the one who found him.

Static. Reuben reaches for a long needle and a loop of tubing. A wave slams the hull. The lamp swings. Reuben shields the wound with his body, then straightens, blood on his forearm, and steadies the table with his knee.

REUBEN
Felix. Can you hold her steady?

FELIX (V.O.)
She's a cargo ship in a gale. She'll do what she wants.

REUBEN
Then pray.

FELIX (V.O.)
Doc, I haven't prayed since '09.

REUBEN
Start.

He slides the needle between the ribs. A wet hiss of air. Colour floods the sailor's face. He breathes, deep and even.

FELIX (V.O.)
Doc? Doc, I heard that. Is he...

REUBEN
He's breathing.

A long silence on the line. Then, thin and cracked, a laugh.

FELIX (V.O.)
Good. Good. I'll tell the captain.

Reuben slumps against the bulkhead. Slides down it until he sits on the deck, hands loose between his knees, blood drying on his cuffs.

REUBEN
(to himself)
Eleven hours.

FELIX (V.O.)
Doc?

REUBEN
Nothing. Keep her steady, Felix.
